From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:53:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lanes flow: fit PR observer to gh latency, real
 approval source, reopen + planner-exemption fixes

Review of PR #3742 @f8971d1278 found three behaviour defects:
1. Reader: 5 s budget vs three 3-4.5 s brokered gh calls per PR returned {} for every PR, and
   approved read reviewDecision (empty on this repo) so merge was unreachable. Now: 30 s
   wall budget, PRs read concurrently (prefetch), view+checks in parallel, approval from a
   non-author human's latest APPROVED review on the current head with no CHANGES_REQUESTED.
2. _review_active ignored review_reopened/reopened: a reopened card still read review.
3. Planner admission dropped the gate_exempt cap exemption (row lacked creator fields);
   row_opts() now feeds reason() in planner, release_due and flow.

Proof: RED 8 failed (new tests) on old code; GREEN 8 consumer files 159 passed, scripts/check 21 ok.
